From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FogCast <build@fogcast.invalid>
Date: Wed, 2 Jul 2025 12:30:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] create_inode: honor fake time for copied inode ctime

When mke2fs populates an image with -d, source inode ctime is copied even
when E2FSPROGS_FAKE_TIME has initialized fs->now. Host ctime cannot be set
by Buildroot's reproducible timestamp pass, so otherwise-identical source
trees produce different images.

Use the existing fake time for ctime when it is configured. Preserve the
current source-stat behavior when it is not.
---
 misc/create_inode.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/misc/create_inode.c b/misc/create_inode.c
index e8bc9cb4..d11a53c1 100644
--- a/misc/create_inode.c
+++ b/misc/create_inode.c
@@ -127,7 +127,7 @@ static errcode_t set_inode_extra(ext2_filsys fs, ext2_ino_t ino,
 	inode.i_mode = (LINUX_S_IFMT & inode.i_mode) | (~S_IFMT & st->st_mode);
 	inode.i_atime = st->st_atime;
 	inode.i_mtime = st->st_mtime;
-	inode.i_ctime = st->st_ctime;
+	inode.i_ctime = fs->now ? fs->now : st->st_ctime;
 
 	retval = ext2fs_write_inode(fs, ino, &inode);
 	if (retval)
-- 
